{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\nd['rationale']=d['rationale']+\\\" Also filed an experiment for the other registered question in this feature: a harness that builds a snapshot at index 1000 plus 9000 committed LogCommand entries above it and constructs the node in both modes. Local construction feedback showed the first fixture attempt with LogNoop entries returned immediately because prepareLog never sends no-ops to the FSM, so the entries were changed to the commit path; the feature-on case then failed to return within the 5s window while the identical fixture with the feature off returned with lastApplied still at the snapshot index, which isolates the replay as the cause.\\\"\nd['sources']=d.get('sources',[])+[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-fsmch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":555,\\\"end_line\\\":562,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-startup-order\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":600,\\\"end_line\\\":640,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}]\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"e99a162d27c7421fa6729d8cb9703581-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_replay_backpressure_test.go\\\",\n \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-restorecommitted\\\",\\\"s-processlogs\\\",\\\"s-fsmch\\\",\\\"s-startup-order\\\",\\\"s-staging\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"A single node (LocalID A) constructed in two modes from the same in-memory stores: a version-1 snapshot at index 1000 with configuration {A} and a log of 9000 committed LogCommand entries above it (indices 1001..10000), with the commit-tracking store reporting commit index 10000; RestoreCommittedLogs off versus on, with normal initialization in both cases.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n    \\\"The fixture is supplied by the harness (snapshot, 9000 entries, staged commit index); it is the restart-shaped state a node running with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled can reach, with the commit index persisted atomically with the log entries by the store contract.\\\",\n    \\\"The number of batches the replay produces is derived from MaxAppendEntries (64) and the entries above the snapshot (9000), giving 141 batches, and is emitted as an operand rather than asserted from a constant.\\\",\n    \\\"Non-return is evaluated by constructing in a goroutine and waiting 5s; the control uses the identical fixture with the feature off, so a slow fixture, slow store or slow FSM is excluded as the cause.\\\",\n    \\\"The feature-on node that never returns cannot be shut down; its goroutine is abandoned when the test process exits.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\": [\n    \\\"No on-disk store is exercised; the in-memory CommitTrackingLogStore is used.\\\",\n    \\\"The blocked constructor is not resumed, so no recovery path after the stall is observed.\\\",\n    \\\"No repository test was executed.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"snapshot_index\\\":1000,\\\"entries_above_snapshot\\\":9000,\\\"log_last_index\\\":10000,\\\"stored_commit_index\\\":10000,\\\"max_append_entries\\\":64,\\\"batches_required\\\":141,\\\"observation_window_seconds\\\":5}\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness builds fresh InmemTransport(\\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\"), InmemStore (stable), InmemCommitTrackingStore (logs) and InmemSnapshotStore (snapshots) per mode; writes a version-1 snapshot at index 1000, term 1 with configuration {A} at configuration index 1 and closes the sink; stores 9000 LogCommand entries at indices 1001..10000 in batches of 256; and calls logs.StageCommitIndex(10000). It then builds Config from DefaultConfig() with LocalID \\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\", a null logger and RestoreCommittedLogs set from the mode, and calls NewRaft(conf, probeFSM, logs, stable, snaps, trans) in a goroutine, emitting a 'construct' event for each mode with the fixture operands (snapshot index, log last index, stored commit index, entries above the snapshot, MaxAppendEntries, batches required and the observation window) and, when the constructor returns, its last applied index, queued FSM batches and the observed FSM mutation channel capacity; when it does not return within the window the event records newraft_returned=false. Modes run in order replay_off, replay_on; the probe FSM discards applied entries and accepts the snapshot bytes.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"hashicorp/raft NewRaft startup path: restoreFromCommittedLogs replays committed entries through processLogs into fsmMutateCh before the constructor starts runFSM.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"e99a162d27c7421fa6729d8cb9703581-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"restoreFromCommittedLogs calls processLogs(commitIndex, nil) before the configuration scan and before background goroutines start\\\"}],\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_replay_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"construct\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"replay_on\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"entries_above_snapshot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":9000},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"batches_required\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":141},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"max_append_entries\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":64},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"stored_commit_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":10000}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_replay_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"construct\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"replay_off\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"entries_above_snapshot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":9000},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"batches_required\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":141},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"max_append_entries\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":64},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"stored_commit_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":10000}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"construct\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_replay_on\\\",\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"replay_on\\\"}],\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"newraft_returned\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"With the replay enabled, construction should return within the observation window.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"construct\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_replay_off\\\",\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"replay_off\\\"}],\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"newraft_returned\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the identical fixture with the feature off should construct normally.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"construct\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_replay_off\\\",\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"replay_off\\\"}],\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"last_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1000},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control operand: without the replay the FSM is not advanced past the snapshot, so the comparison is about the replay and not about the fixture's size.\\\"}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written', len(json.dumps(d)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
